"private to the calling thread, before its file descriptor is installed, so "
"it cannot race a concurrent :manpage:`close(2)`.  Balanced by a matching "
"landlock_free_ruleset event."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:369
msgid "Ruleset freed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:371
msgid ""
"Ruleset being freed (never NULL); at its last reference, so no lock is "
"needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:373
msgid ""
"Emitted when a ruleset's last reference is dropped (typically when the "
"creating process closes the ruleset file descriptor).  Fires even when file-"
"descriptor installation failed after creation, keeping the create/free pair "
"balanced."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:400
msgid "Path-beneath rule added to a ruleset"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:402
#: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:458
msgid "Source ruleset (never NULL)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:404
#: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:460
msgid "``u32 flags``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:403
#: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:459
msgid ""
"Complete validated landlock_add_rule_flags value supplied by this successful "
"call, not the rule's accumulated quiet state."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:406
#: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:462
msgid "``u64 access_rights``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:405
#: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:461
msgid ""
"Canonical per-call access mask passed to landlock_insert_rule() after "
"normalization, not the raw sys_landlock_add_rule() argument or accumulated "
"rule."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:409
#: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:747
msgid "``const struct path *path``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:408
msgid "Filesystem path for the rule (never NULL)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:410
#: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:748
msgid "``const char *pathname``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:409
msgid ""
"Resolved absolute path string (never NULL; error placeholder on resolution "
"failure)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:411
#: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:466
msgid ""
"Emitted by sys_landlock_add_rule() under the modified ruleset's lock, so the "
"reported ruleset is a stable snapshot that no concurrent writer can change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:456
msgid "Network-port rule added to a ruleset"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:465
#: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:697
msgid "``u64 port``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:464
msgid ""
"Network port in host endianness, forwarded directly from :c:type:"
"`landlock_net_port_attr.port <landlock_net_port_attr>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:500
msgid "New domain created"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:506
#: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:553
#: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:646
#: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:697
msgid "``const struct landlock_domain *domain``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:502
msgid ""
"Newly created domain (never NULL, immutable after creation). **domain-"
">hierarchy->id** is its unique ID, shared with the landlock_enforce_domain "
"and landlock_free_domain events; **domain->hierarchy->details** holds the "
"requesting process."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:506
msgid ""
"Source ruleset frozen into the domain (never NULL).  The ruleset lock is "
"held across the emission, so a BPF program reading it via BTF sees the exact "
"merged ruleset; **ruleset->id** / **ruleset->version** identify it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:510
msgid ""
"Emitted by sys_landlock_restrict_self() once, in the requesting thread's "
"context, right after the merge and before thread-sync.  The flags-only path "
"(ruleset_fd == -1) creates no domain and does not emit this event.  Paired "
"with the per-thread landlock_enforce_domain (join on **domain->hierarchy-"
">id**) and balanced by a matching landlock_free_domain event."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:547
msgid "Domain enforced on a thread"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:549
msgid ""
"Domain now enforced on the current thread (never NULL, immutable; read "
"locklessly).  Correlate to landlock_create_domain via **domain->hierarchy-"
">id** for the source ruleset and requesting thread, or read **domain-"
">hierarchy->details** for the requesting process."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:555
msgid "``bool complete``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:554
msgid ""
"Set on the single event that concludes the operation, after all its other "
"enforcements; filter on it for one event per operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:558
msgid "``bool process_wide``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:557
msgid ""
"The enforcement covers every eligible (non-exiting) thread of the process: "
"set when the caller used ``LANDLOCK_RESTRICT_SELF_TSYNC`` or the process is "
"single-threaded.  A lone thread whose group still holds a zombie leader is "
"not counted single-threaded, so process_wide == 0 never proves the opposite."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:564
msgid "``bool no_new_privs``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:563
msgid ""
"The enforcing thread's no_new_privs state at enforcement time: 1 if set (by "
"a prior :manpage:`prctl(2)` ``PR_SET_NO_NEW_PRIVS`` or by "
"``LANDLOCK_RESTRICT_SELF_NO_NEW_PRIVS``), 0 if the domain was enforced with "
"``CAP_SYS_ADMIN`` instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:568
msgid ""
"Emitted for each thread sys_landlock_restrict_self() enforces the domain on, "
"in that thread's own context, right after its commit_creds(), so it fires "
"only once the thread is irreversibly enforcing the domain (aborted "
"operations emit none).  Not balanced; every enforcement falls between the "
"domain's landlock_create_domain and landlock_free_domain events."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:575
msgid ""
"**complete** == 1 && **process_wide** == 1 means the whole process is "
"sandboxed by **domain**, durably (Landlock domains are monotonic and "
"inherited on :manpage:`clone(2)`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:607
msgid "Domain freed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:613
#: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:745
#: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:811
#: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:883
#: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:933
#: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:984
msgid "``const struct landlock_hierarchy *hierarchy``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:609
msgid "Hierarchy node being freed (never NULL)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:610
msgid ""
"Emitted when the hierarchy node's last reference is dropped: its refcount "
"reaches zero after all child domains have released their parent reference.  "
"A committed domain is freed from a kworker via "
"landlock_put_domain_deferred() (the credential free path runs in RCU "
"context, where sleeping is forbidden), so the current task is not the "
"sandboxed task that triggered the free.  Balanced by a matching "
"landlock_create_domain event."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:640
msgid "Inode rule evaluated during access check"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:642
#: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:693
msgid "Enforcing domain (never NULL)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:644
#: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:695
msgid "``const struct landlock_rule *rule``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:643
#: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:694
msgid "Matching rule with per-layer access masks (never NULL)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:645
#: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:696
msgid "``u64 access_request``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:644
msgid ""
"Access mask evaluated against the rule (the domain's handled mask during "
"rename/link double-checks)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:647
msgid "``const struct dentry *dentry``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:646
msgid "Filesystem dentry being checked (never NULL)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:647
msgid ""
"Emitted for each rule that matches during a filesystem access check. The "
"grants array shows the requested rights the rule grants at each domain "
"layer.  See Documentation/trace/events-landlock.rst for how to interpret it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:691
msgid "Network port rule evaluated"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:695
msgid "Access mask being requested."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:696
msgid "Network port being checked (host endianness)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:697
msgid ""
"Emitted for each rule that matches during a network access check.  The "
"grants array shows the requested rights the rule grants at each domain "
"layer.  See Documentation/trace/events-landlock.rst for how to interpret it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:739
msgid "Filesystem access denied"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:741
#: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:807
#: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:879
#: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:930
#: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:981
msgid ""
"Denying domain's hierarchy node (never NULL); its id is the domain field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../trace/events-landlock:323: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:744
#: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:810
#: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:882
#: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:933
#: ../include/trace/events/landlock.h:984
msgid "``bool same_exec``"
msgstr ""

